    "content": "Robert Downey Jr. won his first Academy Award for Best Supporting Actor at the 2024 Oscars for his role as Lewis Strauss in Oppenheimer. This marked his third Oscar nomination and first win, following previous nods for Chaplin (1993) and Tropic Thunder (2009). He was praised for his transformative performance in the film. This video explains why Robert Downey Jr. won an Oscar for this role:59sCinema On TrialYouTube • Sep 9, 2025 59s Key Details Regarding the Oscar Win: Award: Best Supporting Actor (2024). Role: Lewis Strauss in Oppenheimer. Speech Highlights: He thanked his wife, Susan Downey, for her support, joking that she \"portrayed a sane and rational individual who is happily married to an actor\" for 22 years. Significance: This win was widely regarded as a major career milestone, capping a significant comeback. Other 2024 Wins: He also won the Golden Globe, BAFTA, and SAG Award for the same performance in 2024. Oscars 2026 Update: Robert Downey Jr. returned to the 98th Oscars stage on March 15, 2026, with Chris Evans to present an award, notes Deadline. During this appearance, he playfully joked about his 2024 win and engaged in a comedic segment with Chris Evans, according to USA Today.",
